# Mine logs until n are held: a child of `get_wood` so that a mine which cannot
# reach its log (it fails `out_of_reach` or `no_sight`) is ONE failure of the
# caller's rule. A failed primitive is retried by its own rule; a failed child
# skill instead makes the caller's rule ineligible for a tick, and the rules
# below it get their turn. That turn is the climb (`pillar`), see `get_wood`.
skill cut_log(n: int = 1)
  doc "Mine logs of any wood type until n are held; fails with the mine's own kind (out_of_reach, no_sight) when none can be hit."
  rules:
    count(#logs) >= $n -> done
    true -> mine(#logs)
